Here is the commit message:
ACCUMULO-3937 Allow configuration in killing a tserver due to
 HDFS failures

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the lack of configurable parameters for tolerating failures when creating Write-Ahead Log (WAL) files in HDFS. Previously, the system had a hardcoded limit on the number of failures tolerated, which could lead to premature termination of the TabletServer without considering the actual operational requirements or conditions. This inflexibility could result in unnecessary service disruptions during transient HDFS issues.

Here is the patch:

